course: dictionary
lesson: 4732
title: A bird with a huge beak
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hornbill is a bird with a very large, curved beak. Some hornbills have a hard bump on top of the beak, called a casque. You might meet this word in a science text about rainforests, or in a story.
explain: «A hornbill's huge beak is mostly hollow and light.» Huge tells you the beak is very big. Hollow and light tell you it is not heavy, even though it is big. The words around a new word give you clues to its meaning.
explain: «A female hornbill seals herself into a tree hole with mud.» Seals here means closes tightly, so nothing can get in. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: she closes herself in with mud. Does that still make sense? Then it works.
fact: A hornbill is a tropical bird from Africa and Asia.
fact: A hornbill has a very large, curved beak, and some have a hard bump on top called a casque.
fact: Hornbills eat fruit and insects, and they help forests grow by spreading seeds.
fact: In «The Lion King», Zazu is a hornbill, but real hornbills do not talk.
fact: Hornbill is a noun: one hornbill, two hornbills.
exercise: What is a hornbill? | A tall tree that grows in the rainforest | A large fish that lives in the sea | *A tropical bird with a very large, curved beak
exercise: «A female hornbill seals herself into a tree hole with mud.» What does seals mean here? | Eats all the mud | Shows that the tree is very old | *Closes tightly, so nothing can get in | Paints the tree bright colours
exercise: Zazu in The Lion King is a hornbill. Do real hornbills talk like Zazu? | Yes, every hornbill can talk like a person | Yes, but only when it is raining | *No, real hornbills do not talk like Zazu
test: What is the hard bump on top of some hornbills' beaks called? | Talon | Feather | *Casque | Crest
test: What do hornbills help forests do, by eating fruit and spreading seeds? | Freeze in winter | Shrink | *Grow | Turn into rivers
exam: Hornbill is a noun, so which word shows more than one bird? | hornbilled | hornbilling | *hornbills | hornbill's
